Vercel Web Analytics Installation - Implementation Report

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated package.json to include @vercel/analytics as a dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the new dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
Modified: `blog/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the `{children}` element
- This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router integration

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the latest official Vercel documentation from:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

For Next.js App Router projects, the Analytics component should be:
1. Imported from '@vercel/analytics/next'
2. Placed inside the body tag of the root layout
3. Positioned after the main content (children)

This configuration ensures analytics tracking is available across all pages in the application.

## Verification Completed

✓ Build: Successfully compiled with `npm run build`
  - No TypeScript errors
  - All pages generated correctly (7/7 routes)
  - Production build completed in ~17 seconds

✓ Linter: Passed with no errors using `npm run lint`

✓ Lock Files: Updated package-lock.json to reflect the new dependency

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics on Vercel:
1. Navigate to the Vercel dashboard's Analytics section
2. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
3. Deploy the application to Vercel
4. After deployment, analytics data will start appearing in the dashboard

The Analytics component will automatically inject the necessary tracking scripts at `/_vercel/insights/*` routes once enabled on the Vercel platform.
